{
  "title": "Minimum WHS Control Standards",
  "abstract": "The Minimum WHS Control Standards document supplements MRWA Specification 203 and establishes the mandatory work health and safety requirements for all traffic management work conducted under MRWA contracts. This specification sets out the minimum controls that must be implemented on MRWA projects.\n\nThe document covers personal protective equipment (PPE) requirements, site establishment procedures, hazard identification and risk assessment processes, emergency response planning, and incident reporting requirements. It establishes the minimum competency requirements for personnel and specifies the documentation that must be maintained on site.\n\nFor Traffic Controllers and traffic management companies working on MRWA projects, this specification is mandatory reading. It forms part of the contract documents and compliance is required for contractual compliance in addition to WHS legal requirements. The standards are designed to integrate with the WHS Act 2020 and supporting regulations.",
